Common CI/CD issues every DevOps engineer faces (but interviews LOVE them)

CI/CD pipelines don’t fail because of tools. They fail because of design gaps.

Here are the most common CI/CD problems I see in real projects 👇

Pipelines break after small code changes
Secrets exposed in logs or configs
Long build times killing developer productivity
Flaky tests blocking releases
No rollback strategy in production
Same pipeline for dev, staging & prod (no control)
Manual approvals everywhere (no trust, no automation)
Pipelines succeed but deployments fail

💡 What strong DevOps engineers do differently:

 Make pipelines idempotent
 Separate build, test, and deploy stages clearly
 Store secrets in secure vaults (not YAML files)
 Add quality gates, not manual gates
 Design rollback before release
 Treat CI/CD as production code

If your pipeline:
• Works only on “good days”
• Needs constant babysitting
• Breaks under scale
It’s time to redesign — not patch.
